<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.165 percent from 10.198 percent at the previous auction on November 19.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in Egyptian pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 25, 1997 (May 20, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.165 percent (10.198)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 926.975 milion (874.875 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.546 billion (946.225 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.101-10.180 percent (10.101-10.240)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.101-10.331 percent (10.101-10.400)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 66 (123)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 165 (137)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
